// The `++` mirror of `err_bare_plus_operator`: `++` is recognized as an operator
// spelling, but like `+` it has no bare form — incrementing adds 1, so it has
// the same wrapping/saturating choice to make and the same aliased import.
// Never referenced on purpose, so `#[allow]` squelches the unused-import lint.
import { ++ } from builtins; #[allow]

fn main() {}
--- errors ---
